<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/aidrin-hiniduma-2024/inst-aidrin> a airkg:Instrument ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:aidrin-hiniduma-2024 ;
    airkg:grounding_span "To provide a quantifiable assessment of the readiness of data for AI processes, we define parameters of data readiness for AI and introduce AIDRIN (AI Data Readiness INspector).",
        "introduce AIDRIN (AI Data" ;
    airkg:location "Abstract" ;
    airkg:measures <https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/aidrin-hiniduma-2024/c-completeness>,
        <https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/aidrin-hiniduma-2024/c-correlation>,
        <https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/aidrin-hiniduma-2024/c-duplicates>,
        <https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/aidrin-hiniduma-2024/c-fair>,
        <https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/aidrin-hiniduma-2024/c-fairness>,
        <https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/aidrin-hiniduma-2024/c-featimportance>,
        <https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/aidrin-hiniduma-2024/c-outliers> ;
    airkg:method "Quantitative and qualitative assessment of datasets via readiness metrics (completeness, outliers, duplicates, privacy, correlations, fairness, FAIR compliance, class imbalance, feature importance) with visualizations and JSON reports, delivered through a Flask web interface and a PyPI package.",
        "Quantitative readiness metrics and visualizations over tabular data via Flask/Pandas/Matplotlib/Scikit-learn." ;
    airkg:name "AIDRIN (AI Data Readiness Inspector)" ;
    airkg:owner "Hiniduma, Byna, Bez, and Madduri (Ohio State University, Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory, Argonne National Laboratory)",
        "The Ohio State University / LBNL / Argonne National Laboratory" ;
