<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-accrual> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "A DCAT-US metadata field describing how often a dataset is updated. Must use ISO 8601 duration codes in repeating interval format (such as R/P1W for weekly, R/P1M for monthly, R/P1Y for annual) or the literal value 'irregular' for datasets that are no longer updated. Plain English descriptions like 'Weekly' or 'Monthly' are not accepted and cause validation failures." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "accrualPeriodicity" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "A DCAT-US metadata field describing how often a dataset is updated. Must use ISO 8601 duration codes in repeating interval format (such as R/P1W for weekly, R/P1M for monthly, R/P1Y for annual) or the literal value 'irregular' for datasets that are no longer updated. Plain English descriptions like 'Weekly' or 'Monthly' are not accepted and cause validation failures." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-api> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "An application programming interface, which is a set of definitions of the ways one piece of computer software communicates with another. It is a method of achieving abstraction, usually (but not necessarily) between higher-level and lower-level software." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "industry" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "API" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "An application programming interface, which is a set of definitions of the ways one piece of computer software communicates with another. It is a method of achieving abstraction, usually (but not necessarily) between higher-level and lower-level software." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-contactpoint-email> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "A required DCAT-US metadata field containing the email address for the dataset contact. Must be formatted as a single mailto: URI (for example, mailto:contact@agency.gov) with no extra text, no subject lines, no multiple addresses, and no trailing spaces. Common validation failures include appended subject lines, multiple email addresses in one field, or invisible Unicode characters from copy-pasting." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "contactPoint.hasEmail" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "A required DCAT-US metadata field containing the email address for the dataset contact. Must be formatted as a single mailto: URI (for example, mailto:contact@agency.gov) with no extra text, no subject lines, no multiple addresses, and no trailing spaces. Common validation failures include appended subject lines, multiple email addresses in one field, or invisible Unicode characters from copy-pasting." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-data-asset> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "A collection of data elements or datasets that make sense to group together. Each community of interest identifies the Data Assets specific to supporting the needs of their respective mission or business functions. Notably, a Data Asset is a deliberately abstract concept. A given Data Asset may represent an entire database consisting of multiple distinct entity classes, or may represent a single entity class." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "industry" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "Data Asset" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "A collection of data elements or datasets that make sense to group together. Each community of interest identifies the Data Assets specific to supporting the needs of their respective mission or business functions. Notably, a Data Asset is a deliberately abstract concept. A given Data Asset may represent an entire database consisting of multiple distinct entity classes, or may represent a single entity class." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-dataservice> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "describes an API or other programmatic interface that provides access to data" ;
    airkg:location "What's new in v3.0" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "DataService" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "describes an API or other programmatic interface that provides access to data" .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-dataset> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "A dataset is an organized collection of data. The most basic representation of a dataset is data elements presented in tabular form. Each column represents a particular variable. Each row corresponds to a given value of that column’s variable. A dataset may also present information in a variety of non-tabular formats, such as an extensible mark-up language (XML) file, a geospatial data file, or an image file, etc." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "industry" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "Dataset" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "A dataset is an organized collection of data. The most basic representation of a dataset is data elements presented in tabular form. Each column represents a particular variable. Each row corresponds to a given value of that column’s variable. A dataset may also present information in a variety of non-tabular formats, such as an extensible mark-up language (XML) file, a geospatial data file, or an image file, etc." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-datasetseries> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "groups related datasets published over time — annual releases, recurring surveys, versioned reference data — under a single series record." ;
    airkg:location "What's new in v3.0" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "DatasetSeries" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "groups related datasets published over time — annual releases, recurring surveys, versioned reference data — under a single series record." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-dcat-us> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "Data Catalog Vocabulary - United States. The federal metadata standard that data.gov requires for all published datasets. DCAT-US defines which metadata fields are required (such as title, description, modified date, and keywords) and what formats are acceptable for each field. Harvest validation errors occur when dataset metadata does not conform to the DCAT-US schema." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "DCAT-US" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "Data Catalog Vocabulary - United States. The federal metadata standard that data.gov requires for all published datasets. DCAT-US defines which metadata fields are required (such as title, description, modified date, and keywords) and what formats are acceptable for each field. Harvest validation errors occur when dataset metadata does not conform to the DCAT-US schema." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-harvest-job> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "A single run of the harvest process for one harvest source. Each job records how many dataset records were checked, how many were added or updated successfully, and how many encountered errors. When a harvest error notification is sent, it includes a link to the specific harvest job that found the problem." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "industry" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "Harvest Job" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "A single run of the harvest process for one harvest source. Each job records how many dataset records were checked, how many were added or updated successfully, and how many encountered errors. When a harvest error notification is sent, it includes a link to the specific harvest job that found the problem." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-harvest-source> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "A configured connection between harvest.data.gov and an agency's data catalog. Each harvest source specifies where to find the agency's metadata (URL), what format it is in (JSON, XML, ISO 19115, etc.), and how often to check for updates. Each agency typically has one or more harvest sources." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "industry" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "Harvest Source" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "A configured connection between harvest.data.gov and an agency's data catalog. Each harvest source specifies where to find the agency's metadata (URL), what format it is in (JSON, XML, ISO 19115, etc.), and how often to check for updates. Each agency typically has one or more harvest sources." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-harvesting> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "The automated process that pulls dataset metadata from federal agency catalogs into data.gov on a scheduled basis. Instead of agencies manually submitting datasets one by one, the harvester visits each agency's catalog regularly and imports the latest dataset information automatically." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "industry" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "Harvesting" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "The automated process that pulls dataset metadata from federal agency catalogs into data.gov on a scheduled basis. Instead of agencies manually submitting datasets one by one, the harvester visits each agency's catalog regularly and imports the latest dataset information automatically." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-iso-19115> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "An international standard for geospatial metadata. Some federal agencies publish their dataset metadata in ISO 19115 or ISO 19115-2 format. When harvesting these sources, the system converts the ISO metadata into DCAT-US format. Transformation errors can occur if the ISO records are missing required elements that are needed for the conversion." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "ISO 19115" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "An international standard for geospatial metadata. Some federal agencies publish their dataset metadata in ISO 19115 or ISO 19115-2 format. When harvesting these sources, the system converts the ISO metadata into DCAT-US format. Transformation errors can occur if the ISO records are missing required elements that are needed for the conversion." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-iso-8601> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "The international standard for representing dates and times. ISO 8601 requires dates to be formatted as YYYY-MM-DD with hyphens separating year, month, and day (for example, 2024-03-15). Date format errors are the most common type of harvest validation failure, typically occurring when dates are malformed such as having the year and month run together (201603-01 instead of 2016-03-01)." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "ISO 8601" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "The international standard for representing dates and times. ISO 8601 requires dates to be formatted as YYYY-MM-DD with hyphens separating year, month, and day (for example, 2024-03-15). Date format errors are the most common type of harvest validation failure, typically occurring when dates are malformed such as having the year and month run together (201603-01 instead of 2016-03-01)." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-issued> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "An optional DCAT-US metadata field containing the date a dataset was first published or released. When present, must be formatted in ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD). Like the modified field, issued dates commonly fail validation when the year and month are run together without proper hyphen separators." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "issued (metadata field)" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "An optional DCAT-US metadata field containing the date a dataset was first published or released. When present, must be formatted in ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD). Like the modified field, issued dates commonly fail validation when the year and month are run together without proper hyphen separators." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-json-ld> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "JSON Based Serialization for Linked Data. JSON-LD gives Schema.org data about your content to search engines." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "industry" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "JSON-LD" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "JSON Based Serialization for Linked Data. JSON-LD gives Schema.org data about your content to search engines." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-keyword> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "A required DCAT-US metadata field containing tags that describe the dataset's subject matter to help users find it in search results. Must be formatted as an array of strings, even if there is only one keyword (for example, ['environment'] not 'environment'). Datasets must have at least one keyword. Both missing keywords and improperly formatted keyword fields cause validation failures." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "keyword (metadata field)" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "A required DCAT-US metadata field containing tags that describe the dataset's subject matter to help users find it in search results. Must be formatted as an array of strings, even if there is only one keyword (for example, ['environment'] not 'environment'). Datasets must have at least one keyword. Both missing keywords and improperly formatted keyword fields cause validation failures." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-license> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "A DCAT-US metadata field that must contain a URL pointing to the dataset's license document. The field only accepts valid URIs, not plain text descriptions. For most U.S. government public domain datasets, the correct value is https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/. Text values like 'Public Domain' or 'None' cause validation failures." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "license (metadata field)" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "A DCAT-US metadata field that must contain a URL pointing to the dataset's license document. The field only accepts valid URIs, not plain text descriptions. For most U.S. government public domain datasets, the correct value is https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/. Text values like 'Public Domain' or 'None' cause validation failures." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-machine-readable> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "Refers to information or data that is in a format that can be easily processed by a computer without human intervention while ensuring no semantic meaning is lost." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "industry" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "Machine Readable File" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "Refers to information or data that is in a format that can be easily processed by a computer without human intervention while ensuring no semantic meaning is lost." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-metadata> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "These characteristics of data are known as “metadata”, that is, “data that describes data.”" ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "industry" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "Metadata" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "These characteristics of data are known as “metadata”, that is, “data that describes data.”" .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-modified> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "A required DCAT-US metadata field containing the date a dataset or its metadata was last updated. Must be formatted in ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD). The most common harvest error is a malformed modified date where the year and month run together without the required hyphen separator. Missing modified dates also trigger validation failures since this is a required field." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "modified (metadata field)" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "A required DCAT-US metadata field containing the date a dataset or its metadata was last updated. Must be formatted in ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD). The most common harvest error is a malformed modified date where the year and month run together without the required hyphen separator. Missing modified dates also trigger validation failures since this is a required field." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-open-standard> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "A standard developed or adopted by voluntary consensus standards bodies, both domestic and international. These standards include provisions requiring that owners of relevant intellectual property have agreed to make that intellectual property available on a non-discriminatory, royalty-free or reasonable royalty basis to all interested parties." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "industry" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "Open Standard" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "A standard developed or adopted by voluntary consensus standards bodies, both domestic and international. These standards include provisions requiring that owners of relevant intellectual property have agreed to make that intellectual property available on a non-discriminatory, royalty-free or reasonable royalty basis to all interested parties." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-transformation-error> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "A harvest error that occurs before validation when the harvester cannot read or convert a metadata record at all. These indicate structural problems with the source file itself, such as malformed XML, missing required elements in ISO 19115 records, or unrecognizable record structures. Transformation errors make up approximately 32% of harvest failures and always begin with the phrase 'record failed to transform'." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "industry" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "Transformation Error" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "A harvest error that occurs before validation when the harvester cannot read or convert a metadata record at all. These indicate structural problems with the source file itself, such as malformed XML, missing required elements in ISO 19115 records, or unrecognizable record structures. Transformation errors make up approximately 32% of harvest failures and always begin with the phrase 'record failed to transform'." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/dcat-us-3-overview/def-validation-error> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:dcat-us-3-overview ;
    airkg:grounding_span "A harvest error that occurs when a metadata field value does not conform to the DCAT-US schema requirements. The harvester can read the record, but a specific field value is formatted incorrectly, contains an unacceptable value, or is missing when required. Validation errors make up approximately 66% of all harvest failures. These errors typically begin with a field name such as '$.modified' or '$.accrualPeriodicity'." ;
    airkg:location "Glossary" ;
    airkg:normative_status "industry" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "73fc00613a8649b18a91a04497c82423" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.3" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "87d3d2a8bb9d8ddc445e6674b4738e58f6b0d8629f6d19093dfc360b90175fa0" ;
    airkg:term "Validation Error" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "A harvest error that occurs when a metadata field value does not conform to the DCAT-US schema requirements. The harvester can read the record, but a specific field value is formatted incorrectly, contains an unacceptable value, or is missing when required. Validation errors make up approximately 66% of all harvest failures. These errors typically begin with a field name such as '$.modified' or '$.accrualPeriodicity'." .

