    airkg:verbatim_text "The term ‘identifiable form’ means any representation of information that permits the identity of the respondent to whom the information applies to be reasonably inferred by either direct or indirect means." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/foundations-for-evidence-based-policymaking-act-of-2018-evid/d19> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:foundations-for-evidence-based-policymaking-act-of-2018-evid ;
    airkg:as_of_date "2019-01-14" ;
    airkg:grounding_span "means the use of data in identifiable form for" ;
    airkg:location "§3561(8), 132 STAT. 5545" ;
    airkg:normative_status "statute" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "38e0c9aaa4214cfa9e0a96788bcb29cc" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.2" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "9a9869d01c9a078376bd8e701b7657449f17e921036d6b24d7b03bb0c255c27e" ;
    airkg:term "nonstatistical purpose" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "The term ‘nonstatistical purpose’— (A) means the use of data in identifiable form for any purpose that is not a statistical purpose, including any administrative, regulatory, law enforcement, adjudicatory, or other purpose that affects the rights, privileges, or benefits of a particular identifiable respondent; and (B) includes the disclosure under section 552 of title 5 of data that are acquired for exclusively statistical purposes under a pledge of confidentiality." .

