<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/statistical-policy-working-paper-46-data-quality-assessment/d1> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:statistical-policy-working-paper-46-data-quality-assessment ;
    airkg:as_of_date "2013-02" ;
    airkg:grounding_span "Broadly defined, data quality means" ;
    airkg:location "Introduction" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "534f7cc019534bfc94a219f9ee81789c" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.2" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "1b1f030dbb7eb9c46e4e8e03c0411ffab6f715d7332dafe7f92aead92c4ed936" ;
    airkg:term "data quality" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "Broadly defined, data quality means \"fitness for use.\"" .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/statistical-policy-working-paper-46-data-quality-assessment/d2> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:statistical-policy-working-paper-46-data-quality-assessment ;
    airkg:as_of_date "2013-02" ;
    airkg:grounding_relocated_from "Relevance refers to how well the administrative data file meets the needs of the" ;
    airkg:grounding_relocation_method "deterministic" ;
    airkg:grounding_span "Relevance refers to how well the administrative data file meets the needs of the user in regards to data level (person, family, household, establishment, company, etc.), broad data definitions and concepts, population coverage, time period and timeliness." ;
    airkg:location "Discovery Phase" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "534f7cc019534bfc94a219f9ee81789c" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.2" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "1b1f030dbb7eb9c46e4e8e03c0411ffab6f715d7332dafe7f92aead92c4ed936" ;
    airkg:term "Relevance" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "Relevance refers to how well the administrative data file meets the needs of the user in regards to data level (person, family, household, establishment, company, etc.), broad data definitions and concepts, population coverage, time period and timeliness." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/statistical-policy-working-paper-46-data-quality-assessment/d3> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:statistical-policy-working-paper-46-data-quality-assessment ;
    airkg:as_of_date "2013-02" ;
    airkg:grounding_relocated_from "Accessibility refers to the ease with which the data file extract can be" ;
    airkg:grounding_relocation_method "deterministic" ;
    airkg:grounding_span "Accessibility refers to the ease with which the data file extract can be obtained from the administrative agency. This includes the suitability of the form or medium for transferring the data, confidentiality constraints, and cost." ;
    airkg:location "Discovery Phase" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "534f7cc019534bfc94a219f9ee81789c" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.2" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "1b1f030dbb7eb9c46e4e8e03c0411ffab6f715d7332dafe7f92aead92c4ed936" ;
    airkg:term "Accessibility" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "Accessibility refers to the ease with which the data file extract can be obtained from the administrative agency. This includes the suitability of the form or medium for transferring the data, confidentiality constraints, and cost." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/statistical-policy-working-paper-46-data-quality-assessment/d4> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:statistical-policy-working-paper-46-data-quality-assessment ;
    airkg:as_of_date "2013-02" ;
    airkg:grounding_relocated_from "Coherence refers to the degree to which the administrative data are comparable with" ;
    airkg:grounding_relocation_method "deterministic" ;
    airkg:grounding_span "Coherence refers to the degree to which the administrative data are comparable with other data sources and consistent over time and across geographical areas." ;
    airkg:location "Initial Acquisition Phase" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "534f7cc019534bfc94a219f9ee81789c" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.2" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "1b1f030dbb7eb9c46e4e8e03c0411ffab6f715d7332dafe7f92aead92c4ed936" ;
    airkg:term "Coherence" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "Coherence refers to the degree to which the administrative data are comparable with other data sources and consistent over time and across geographical areas." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/statistical-policy-working-paper-46-data-quality-assessment/d5> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:statistical-policy-working-paper-46-data-quality-assessment ;
    airkg:as_of_date "2013-02" ;
    airkg:grounding_relocated_from "Interpretability refers to the clarity of information to ensure that the" ;
    airkg:grounding_relocation_method "deterministic" ;
    airkg:grounding_span "Interpretability refers to the clarity of information to ensure that the administrative data are utilized in an appropriate way. This includes evaluation of data collection forms, data collection instructions, and a data dictionary." ;
    airkg:location "Discovery Phase" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "534f7cc019534bfc94a219f9ee81789c" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.2" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "1b1f030dbb7eb9c46e4e8e03c0411ffab6f715d7332dafe7f92aead92c4ed936" ;
    airkg:term "Interpretability" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "Interpretability refers to the clarity of information to ensure that the administrative data are utilized in an appropriate way. This includes evaluation of data collection forms, data collection instructions, and a data dictionary." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/statistical-policy-working-paper-46-data-quality-assessment/d6> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:statistical-policy-working-paper-46-data-quality-assessment ;
    airkg:as_of_date "2013-02" ;
    airkg:grounding_relocated_from "Accuracy refers to the closeness of the administrative record data values to their" ;
    airkg:grounding_relocation_method "deterministic" ;
    airkg:grounding_span "Accuracy refers to the closeness of the administrative record data values to their (unknown) true values. This includes information on any known sources of errors in the administrative data such as missing records, missing values of individual data items, misinterpretation of questions, and keying, coding, and duplication errors." ;
    airkg:location "Initial Acquisition Phase" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "534f7cc019534bfc94a219f9ee81789c" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.2" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "1b1f030dbb7eb9c46e4e8e03c0411ffab6f715d7332dafe7f92aead92c4ed936" ;
    airkg:term "Accuracy" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "Accuracy refers to the closeness of the administrative record data values to their (unknown) true values. This includes information on any known sources of errors in the administrative data such as missing records, missing values of individual data items, misinterpretation of questions, and keying, coding, and duplication errors." .

<https://brockwebb.github.io/ai-readiness-kg/doc/statistical-policy-working-paper-46-data-quality-assessment/d7> a airkg:Definition ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom doc:statistical-policy-working-paper-46-data-quality-assessment ;
    airkg:as_of_date "2013-02" ;
    airkg:grounding_span "Institutional Environment refers to the credibility of the" ;
    airkg:location "Initial Acquisition Phase" ;
    airkg:normative_status "standard" ;
    airkg:prov_extraction_event_id "534f7cc019534bfc94a219f9ee81789c" ;
    airkg:prov_model_id "claude-opus-4-8" ;
    airkg:prov_schema_version "0.2" ;
    airkg:prov_source_sha256 "1b1f030dbb7eb9c46e4e8e03c0411ffab6f715d7332dafe7f92aead92c4ed936" ;
    airkg:term "Institutional Environment" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "Institutional Environment refers to the credibility of the administrative agency for producing high quality and reliable administrative data. This includes an evaluation of the agency's quality standards and processes for assuring adherence to standards." .

