    airkg:term "Distribution" ;
    airkg:verbatim_text "A distribution represents a specific available form of a dataset. Each dataset might be available in different forms; these forms might represent different formats of the dataset or different endpoints. Examples of distributions include a downloadable CSV file, an API or an RSS feed" .

